"Elias, called the Informant, is an old man who runs the information business on Apex."
"He lives in a brick townhouse facing a grassy square, with a silver-muzzled golden retriever."
"He supplies SkySea Guard with infogear, the island's spy-grade devices."
"An AI-like creation of his, with a soothing male voice, synthesizes his information."
"He says he doesn't hold himself to the System's privacy standards."
"He sells SkySea Guard information on runaway Avowed."
"He is an old high-rank Wright; his son is Techno Tarek."
"His square near Sānjiǎo Beach has a jar-shaped fountain that anchors his network."
"Over eight decades he built keys of voices, hidden in walls and in the infogear he sells."
"Through the fountain his skill hears live conversations anywhere through every key at once."
"He won't sell this creation to the Triplanets, but will negotiate its use and protection."
"In the Matadero flood he lent helicopters and sent phones to Vandy's shelter."
"His creation MBF stores simulations of people to predict them; it rejected other names."
"From his keys he can raise a phantasm of a person to question; they are not spirits."
"He offers ten million Argold to anyone who steals from him without being caught."
"Triplanet investigators and even Artonans turn to him for intelligence."
"He knows Aulia Velra intimately and calls her woo-woo woman."
"Episode 473 of his Saturday Morning Show was about Alden Thorn."
"He locked information requests on Alden for eleven months as a thank-you."
